{"name":"Monte Carlo","hex":"#7ac5b4","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Monte Carlo","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A ward of Monaco, Europe, famous for its casinos.","Ellipsis of Monte Carlo method."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A commonly served drink consisting of beer and grenadine.","An informal dance competition, where contestants in one quarter of the floor are eliminated by a randomly drawn card representing the corner."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Monte_Carlo"}],"entries":[{"title":"Monte Carlo","blocks":[{"text":"Monte Carlo is an official administrative area of Monaco, specifically the ward of Monte Carlo/Spélugues. Informally, the name also refers to a larger district, the Monte Carlo Quarter, which besides Monte Carlo/Spélugues also includes the wards of La Rousse/Saint Roman, Larvotto/Bas Moulins and Saint Michel. The permanent population of the ward of Monte Carlo is about 3,500, while that of the quarter is about 15,000. Monaco has four traditional quarters; from west to east they are Fontvieille, Monaco-Ville, La Condamine, and Monte Carlo."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/da/Panorama_von_Monaco-La_Turbie.jpg/330px-Panorama_von_Monaco-La_Turbie.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Monte_Carlo","wikidata":"Q45240"},{"title":"Monte Carlo (2011 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Monte Carlo is a 2011 American adventure-romantic comedy film based on the 2001 novel Headhunters by Rankin/Bass co-founder Jules Bass. It was directed by Thomas Bezucha. Denise Di Novi, Alison Greenspan, Nicole Kidman, and Arnon Milchan produced the film for Fox 2000 Pictures and Regency Enterprises. It began production in Harghita, Romania on May 5, 2010."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/b/b2/Monte_Carlo_Poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Monte_Carlo_(2011_film)","wikidata":"Q550248"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/31/CharlesIIIMonaco.jpg/500px-CharlesIIIMonaco.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/31/CharlesIIIMonaco.jpg/500px-CharlesIIIMonaco.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Charles III of Monaco was responsible for turning the Monte Carlo district and Monaco into a thriving town.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACharlesIIIMonaco.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c9/Eglise_st_charles_Monaco_b.jpg/500px-Eglise_st_charles_Monaco_b.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c9/Eglise_st_charles_Monaco_b.jpg/1280px-Eglise_st_charles_Monaco_b.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c9/Eglise_st_charles_Monaco_b.jpg/500px-Eglise_st_charles_Monaco_b.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"St Charles Church, Monte Carlo","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEglise_st_charles_Monaco_b.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/Le_casino_de_Monte-Carlo.JPG/500px-Le_casino_de_Monte-Carlo.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/Le_casino_de_Monte-Carlo.JPG/1280px-Le_casino_de_Monte-Carlo.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/Le_casino_de_Monte-Carlo.JPG/500px-Le_casino_de_Monte-Carlo.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Monte Car